WEBVTT

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:21.660
Anne?

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:23.040
Anne!

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:24.160
What?

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:26.390
J-Jonas?

00:01:57.710 --> 00:01:59.590
What happened, Jonas?

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:02.320
What are you doing here?

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:05.500
I was worried, so I came after you.

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:06.880
I'm glad you're safe.

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:09.310
From here on, I'll protect you.

00:02:09.310 --> 00:02:13.860
I'm not sure that means much coming from
 someone who was just attacked by bandits...

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:16.010
But it's very strange...

00:02:16.010 --> 00:02:18.320
When did I catch up and pass you?

00:02:18.790 --> 00:02:22.480
I stopped in the town of Redington, so...

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:24.680
Wait, are you even listening to me?

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:25.540
Redington?

00:02:25.870 --> 00:02:28.860
Oh, that's where you 
bought the warrior fairy.

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:30.250
It's quite beautiful.

00:02:30.650 --> 00:02:33.460
Did you make a mistake 
and buy a companion fairy instead?

00:02:34.530 --> 00:02:38.090
Jonas, please, won't you go back?

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:40.760
This journey is much too dangerous for you.

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:42.260
I am not going back.

00:02:43.160 --> 00:02:45.530
I am going to Lewiston with you.

00:02:45.530 --> 00:02:47.290
And you know why, don't you?

00:02:47.290 --> 00:02:48.890
Because I love you!

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:51.120
Um, Jonas.

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:55.530
I appreciate your feelings, 
but I think you're confused.

00:02:55.530 --> 00:02:58.780
You think the feelings of pity 
you have toward me are love.

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:01.070
I came here for your sake!

00:03:01.070 --> 00:03:03.120
Do you hate me?

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:04.490
This doesn't make you happy at all?

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:11.040
Scarecrow. We should hurry 
and leave this place.

00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:13.080
Wild crows.

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:15.150
They've caught the scent 
of blood and come here.

00:03:15.150 --> 00:03:17.880
Once they've appeared, 
wolves aren't far behind.

00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:20.930
This is bad. We must set off at once!

00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:23.210
So, you have a man who would come after you?

00:03:23.210 --> 00:03:24.890
Impressive, for a child.

00:03:24.890 --> 00:03:26.480
I am not a child!

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:29.600
I am fifteen. I have fully come of age!

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:34.100
And Jonas isn't that sort of a person to me. 
He feels pity for me, that's all.

00:03:34.490 --> 00:03:35.560
Pity?

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:38.540
Whatever the case, 
you should turn back here, Jonas!

00:03:38.540 --> 00:03:42.740
You aren't the sort of person who should be 
doing dangerous things in a place like this!

00:03:55.860 --> 00:03:59.280
Say, Challe. About the cart behind us...

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:02.400
If anything happens, will you go and help?

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:04.440
If you wish to make me do something,

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:06.440
use my wing against me
 and give me an order.

00:04:06.440 --> 00:04:10.060
Earlier, you were quite annoying about saying, 
"Give me an order, give me an order."

00:04:10.060 --> 00:04:11.230
What was that?

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:13.630
Other than what I am ordered to do,

00:04:13.630 --> 00:04:15.190
I intend to do nothing.

00:04:15.190 --> 00:04:18.520
It's true that I decided to 
make you serve me, Challe.

00:04:18.520 --> 00:04:21.370
But I also said that I hate doing that.

00:04:21.370 --> 00:04:23.140
That's why this is a request.

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:25.580
For now, I will continue to make requests.

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:28.540
If you still refuse, 
then I'll change them into orders.

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:29.610
And, just as you wish,

00:04:29.610 --> 00:04:32.840
I'll even say, "I'll rip up your wing 
unless you do as you're told."

00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:35.200
But first, I will make a request!

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:37.630
You truly are a strange scarecrow-head.

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:39.500
You keep saying "scarecrow, scarecrow"...

00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:42.860
Not that it matters anymore.

00:04:44.030 --> 00:04:46.090
So this is a fortshelter, is it?

00:04:46.090 --> 00:04:47.760
It's my first time staying in one.

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:51.500
Your first time? 
Then, what did you do last night?

00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:53.230
I had the horses run through the night.

00:04:53.830 --> 00:04:56.330
I wanted to catch up to you 
as quickly as possible!

00:04:56.330 --> 00:04:59.050
Jonas, after we stay here tonight, 
tomorrow you should—

00:04:59.050 --> 00:05:02.440
Right now, I am simply going 
somewhere I want to go, that's all.

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:05.150
It isn't as though I'm following you.

00:05:07.090 --> 00:05:09.120
My head aches...

00:05:22.760 --> 00:05:24.010
Don't touch me!

00:05:24.010 --> 00:05:26.760
Everything other than what you 
hold in your hands is mine.

00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:35.430
Jonas? It's me. Will you open the door?

00:05:35.900 --> 00:05:37.500
Was there something you required?

00:05:37.500 --> 00:05:38.400
Cathy!

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:40.570
You came with him?

00:05:40.570 --> 00:05:44.360
I am Master Jonas's labor fairy. 
Naturally, I did.

00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:48.510
Th-That's true. Of course. 
And where is Jonas?

00:05:48.510 --> 00:05:50.700
He has retired for the evening.

00:05:50.700 --> 00:05:54.330
Then when he wakes, 
will you tell him to eat this?

00:05:55.430 --> 00:05:59.790
Such crude fare as this... 
Master Jonas will not eat a single mouthful.

00:05:59.790 --> 00:06:02.190
At home, that might be true,

00:06:02.190 --> 00:06:05.260
but on a journey, this is 
something to be grateful for.

00:06:05.260 --> 00:06:08.720
It reeks of beast fat. 
Even I, a fairy, would disdain to eat it.

00:06:09.050 --> 00:06:12.310
Is that so? Well, I'm very sorry 
for my unwanted meddling!

00:06:13.810 --> 00:06:14.700
Here.

00:06:15.140 --> 00:06:17.720
What is it? And what do you 
want me to do with it?

00:06:17.720 --> 00:06:20.090
It's your portion, of course!

00:06:20.090 --> 00:06:22.570
Was it wrong of me 
to offer you such poor fare?

00:06:22.570 --> 00:06:26.060
Does a soup reeking of beast fat 
not suit your taste either?

00:06:26.060 --> 00:06:27.550
What is this, all of a sudden?

00:06:27.550 --> 00:06:29.610
It's as though your head 
has been set on fire.

00:06:29.610 --> 00:06:32.830
Well, I am a scarecrow-head, after all. 
I'm sure it would burn very well!

00:06:33.460 --> 00:06:35.040
Apparently, it's quite the blaze.

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:37.050
Well, who wouldn't be ablaze?

00:06:37.050 --> 00:06:39.050
"This poor person's soup wouldn't suit

00:06:39.050 --> 00:06:41.680
the tastes of an honorable heir 
to a sugar confectionary."

00:06:41.680 --> 00:06:43.550
That's what a fairy just said to me.

00:06:43.550 --> 00:06:45.500
Do you find this soup detestable, too?

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:49.300
That isn't it. I was simply... surprised.

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:52.200
Surprised? By what?

00:06:52.200 --> 00:06:56.120
Before serving yourself, 
you gave me soup. That surprised me.

00:06:56.740 --> 00:06:58.350
What are you talking about?

00:06:58.350 --> 00:07:02.440
When you make food, having other people 
eat first is the normal thing to do, isn't it?

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:03.730
Oh, a spoon!

00:07:07.070 --> 00:07:08.640
I'm so sorry!

00:07:08.640 --> 00:07:09.650
What?

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:19.410
Challe, that was...

00:07:19.410 --> 00:07:20.430
I ate it.

00:07:20.430 --> 00:07:22.600
You ate it? How?

00:07:22.600 --> 00:07:24.640
We don't eat with our mouths.

00:07:24.640 --> 00:07:27.630
We hold our hands over it, 
or touch it, to absorb it.

00:07:27.630 --> 00:07:30.000
Is that how fairies are?

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:31.760
So, was it good?

00:07:31.760 --> 00:07:35.530
There is no flavor. We simply absorb it.

00:07:36.610 --> 00:07:39.220
There is one thing which we can taste.

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:40.180
What is it?

00:07:40.890 --> 00:07:42.140
Silver sugar.

00:07:42.790 --> 00:07:43.670
It's sweet.

00:07:46.160 --> 00:07:48.360
Do you like sugar confections?

00:07:48.750 --> 00:07:49.880
I don't hate them.

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:53.150
Then, I'll make some for you!

00:07:53.150 --> 00:07:56.490
Despite how I might appear, 
I am a bit of a sugar artisan!

00:07:56.490 --> 00:07:57.480
You?

00:07:59.140 --> 00:08:00.940
Listen and be amazed!

00:08:00.940 --> 00:08:03.400
My mama was a silver sugar master!

00:08:03.400 --> 00:08:04.620
As her daughter,

00:08:04.620 --> 00:08:08.670
I've been playing with silver sugar 
instead of clay since I could toddle!

00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:12.180
Moonflower would suit you, Challe. 
Maybe I'll make something in that shape.

00:08:15.320 --> 00:08:17.600
Challe! Th-There's something 
in the cargo hold!

00:08:17.600 --> 00:08:18.800
W-Will you go and look?

00:08:18.800 --> 00:08:20.020
Is that an order?

00:08:20.020 --> 00:08:20.970
What?

00:08:21.290 --> 00:08:24.600
If I don't go look, will you tear up my wing?

00:08:24.600 --> 00:08:26.310
Th-That isn't...

00:08:26.310 --> 00:08:28.270
Then, do it yourself.

00:08:28.270 --> 00:08:31.440
Fine. I'll just go and look then!

00:08:43.570 --> 00:08:45.560
There's nothing here?

00:08:45.560 --> 00:08:46.960
Hey, you!

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:48.810
No!

00:08:49.380 --> 00:08:52.320
Let me go, you lowlife! I said, let go!

00:08:52.320 --> 00:08:53.820
Is this meant as provocation?!

00:08:54.840 --> 00:08:56.110
Owww...

00:08:56.110 --> 00:08:59.320
You sure are a rough one! 
I am delicate, you know?

00:08:59.320 --> 00:09:00.460
Be gentler with me!

00:09:00.460 --> 00:09:01.420
You talk too much.

00:09:02.060 --> 00:09:04.860
So, you're the one who was 
running wild in the cargo hold?

00:09:04.860 --> 00:09:06.590
I wasn't running wild.

00:09:06.590 --> 00:09:09.450
I nodded off, had a nightmare, 
and woke with a jump.

00:09:09.450 --> 00:09:11.390
That was quite a jump as you woke up.

00:09:11.390 --> 00:09:13.370
That aside, who are you?

00:09:13.370 --> 00:09:16.030
When, and why, did you climb into my cart?

00:09:16.660 --> 00:09:18.700
I am Mithril Lid Pod!

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:20.870
I've come to return the favor to you!

00:09:20.870 --> 00:09:22.760
Return the favor?

00:09:22.760 --> 00:09:23.580
Oh!

00:09:23.580 --> 00:09:26.620
Bah! I'd never thank the likes of a human!

00:09:26.620 --> 00:09:28.080
And don't you forget it!

00:09:28.080 --> 00:09:29.790
Are you the one from back then?

00:09:29.790 --> 00:09:32.560
What? So, you didn't remember me?

00:09:32.560 --> 00:09:35.760
Forgetting the face of the one 
you saved... You're heartless!

00:09:35.760 --> 00:09:39.640
Wh-What is that supposed to mean? 
How does that make me heartless?

00:09:39.640 --> 00:09:41.870
Besides, back then, you were 
covered in mud and—

00:09:41.870 --> 00:09:44.750
At any rate, yesterday, you saved me.

00:09:44.750 --> 00:09:47.810
That's why I've come to fulfill my duty.

00:09:47.810 --> 00:09:52.270
But back then, you said you'd never 
thank a human, didn't you?

00:09:52.270 --> 00:09:55.310
I did. Because I hate humans, you see?

00:09:55.310 --> 00:09:57.390
That's why I'm returning the favor instead.

00:09:57.390 --> 00:10:01.280
And let me tell you, I'll return the favor, 
but I'll never say thanks, not even if I die.

00:10:01.280 --> 00:10:02.990
Well then! Let me return the favor!

00:10:03.310 --> 00:10:05.290
Well, um...

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:06.270
I know!

00:10:06.270 --> 00:10:08.410
Will you oil the wagon's axles for me?

00:10:08.410 --> 00:10:09.760
Don't treat me like I'm stupid!

00:10:09.760 --> 00:10:13.260
In return for the favor of saving my life, 
you want me to do something that dull?!

00:10:13.260 --> 00:10:15.340
Think of a more impressive favor!

00:10:15.340 --> 00:10:17.500
What do you mean by "an impressive favor"?

00:10:17.500 --> 00:10:20.410
I'm telling you to figure it out, aren't I?

00:10:20.970 --> 00:10:23.680
He's a fussy one. 
Should I strangle him to death?

00:10:21.910 --> 00:10:25.840
A favor! A favor!

00:10:23.680 --> 00:10:25.590
If you order me to, I will.

00:10:25.840 --> 00:10:26.780
What did you say?

00:10:26.780 --> 00:10:28.140
Wait, wait, wait!

00:10:28.140 --> 00:10:30.280
Then there won't have been 
any point in saving him!

00:10:30.280 --> 00:10:33.320
Let's see, you... Mithril, was it?

00:10:33.320 --> 00:10:36.270
It's Mithril Lid Pod! Don't shorten it!

00:10:37.230 --> 00:10:38.990
Mithril Lid Pod.

00:10:38.990 --> 00:10:41.720
There's no need to return the favor.

00:10:41.720 --> 00:10:44.400
I didn't save you in the hopes of 
something like that.

00:10:44.400 --> 00:10:48.440
You're free. You should go wherever 
you like and live happily th—

00:10:48.440 --> 00:10:50.240
Hey! Human girl!

00:10:50.240 --> 00:10:51.160
It's Anne.

00:10:52.160 --> 00:10:52.860
Anne.

00:10:52.860 --> 00:10:55.680
You're pretending you're kind 
when you're not, trying to get rid of me!

00:10:55.680 --> 00:10:56.880
Like I'll let that happen?

00:10:56.880 --> 00:10:58.000
Let me repay the favor!

00:10:58.000 --> 00:11:01.260
If you don't, I'll follow you 
to the depths of the underworld!

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:02.720
The underworld?

00:11:03.230 --> 00:11:04.540
We should strangle him to death.

00:11:04.540 --> 00:11:05.430
You!

00:11:05.430 --> 00:11:07.950
You're a fairy, too! 
How could you say such mean things to me?

00:11:06.130 --> 00:11:09.390
Somehow, I feel exhausted.

00:11:07.950 --> 00:11:10.760
Fairy killer! Fairy killer!

00:11:10.760 --> 00:11:13.550
Let go of me! Let me go, you fairy killer!

00:11:12.350 --> 00:11:16.170
I'm sorry, Challe. I'll make a sugar 
confection for you tomorrow night.

00:11:13.550 --> 00:11:18.240
Hey! You! I'm talking to you!

00:11:16.170 --> 00:11:19.210
Don't steal your wing 
while I'm asleep, all right?

00:11:18.240 --> 00:11:21.880
Let go! Let go! Let go! Let go! Let go!

00:11:19.210 --> 00:11:22.400
Regardless of whether I take it or not, 
I don't think you will be able to sleep.

00:11:22.400 --> 00:11:25.440
Hey, you two! Why are you 
trying to go to sleep?!

00:11:25.440 --> 00:11:27.480
Wake up! I said, wake up!

00:11:27.480 --> 00:11:30.040
Don't fall asleep!

00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:39.880
Shall we throw him out now, while we can?

00:11:39.880 --> 00:11:42.600
That would be too cruel, so please don't.

00:11:42.600 --> 00:11:45.690
And even if we did cast him aside, 
he'd only come back.

00:11:45.690 --> 00:11:49.100
He did go so far as to say he'd follow us 
to the depths of the underworld.

00:11:51.140 --> 00:11:52.060
<i>Mama...</i>

00:11:52.820 --> 00:11:55.240
<i>Until we reach Lewiston safely...</i>

00:11:55.240 --> 00:11:56.840
<i>please watch over us.</i>

00:12:02.760 --> 00:12:04.990
Anne, you understand, don't you?

00:12:04.990 --> 00:12:07.360
I am worried about you.

00:12:07.360 --> 00:12:08.540
That's all.

00:12:10.600 --> 00:12:11.580
Anne.

00:12:15.720 --> 00:12:18.890
We've traveled 300 karon 
since we started the Bloody Highway.

00:12:18.890 --> 00:12:21.940
From this point on, it would be even more 
dangerous to turn back alone.

00:12:22.630 --> 00:12:25.430
Now it's come to this, why don't we travel 
as far as Lewiston together?

00:12:25.430 --> 00:12:27.140
You understand, then?!

00:12:27.140 --> 00:12:31.280
In return, I hope you understand 
that this is truly dangerous.

00:12:31.280 --> 00:12:32.480
Of course.

00:12:41.480 --> 00:12:44.320
Jonas, Cathy, allow me 
to formally introduce you.

00:12:44.810 --> 00:12:47.400
Challe fen Challe. He's a warrior fairy.

00:12:47.400 --> 00:12:49.550
What about a name? You haven't given him one?

00:12:49.550 --> 00:12:51.450
What I just told you is his name.

00:12:51.450 --> 00:12:53.290
I call him Challe.

00:12:53.290 --> 00:12:56.540
Normally, you give them human names.

00:12:56.540 --> 00:13:01.280
You there. You're so beautiful it seems 
a waste to keep you as a warrior fairy.

00:13:01.280 --> 00:13:03.420
You'd be likely to sell as a companion fairy.

00:13:03.420 --> 00:13:06.510
If I suit your fancy, then will you 
buy me from the scarecrow?

00:13:06.510 --> 00:13:09.440
In terms of foolishness, 
you're each as bad as the other.

00:13:09.440 --> 00:13:12.020
It doesn't matter to me 
which of you I am made to serve.

00:13:12.020 --> 00:13:13.850
F-Foolishness?

00:13:13.850 --> 00:13:14.970
Challe!

00:13:14.970 --> 00:13:18.380
I'm sorry, Jonas! Challe has a sharp tongue.

00:13:18.380 --> 00:13:22.180
He's called me an idiot 
or a fool countless times.

00:13:22.180 --> 00:13:24.110
Please don't let it bother you.

00:13:24.110 --> 00:13:27.580
I-I won't. It isn't something 
you need to apologize for, Anne.

00:13:27.580 --> 00:13:30.080
More importantly, what about that fairy?

00:13:30.080 --> 00:13:31.590
You mean me?

00:13:31.590 --> 00:13:34.460
I am Lord Mithril Lid Pod!

00:13:34.460 --> 00:13:36.540
Make sure to use "lord" 
when you call my name.

00:13:36.540 --> 00:13:38.250
L-Lord?

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:39.530
Honestly!

00:13:39.530 --> 00:13:42.300
Why are both of you so arrogant?

00:13:42.300 --> 00:13:46.680
Please confine that attitude just to me. 
Other people have nothing to do with it!

00:13:46.680 --> 00:13:48.470
Now, it's time for our meal!

00:13:52.990 --> 00:13:57.440
With so much delicious food, you wouldn't 
need something like my soup, would you?

00:13:57.440 --> 00:14:01.920
Of course not. Not that crude soup 
reeking of beast fat.

00:14:01.920 --> 00:14:03.400
Silence, Cathy!

00:14:03.400 --> 00:14:07.360
I will not allow you to speak 
to Anne with such rudeness!

00:14:08.200 --> 00:14:10.740
My apologies, Master Jonas. I was only—

00:14:10.740 --> 00:14:12.200
Disappear.

00:14:16.160 --> 00:14:20.540
I'm sorry, Anne. My labor fairy 
hasn't been trained very well.

00:14:20.990 --> 00:14:24.750
Your soup was delicious. 
I would be happy to have it again tonight.

00:14:24.750 --> 00:14:26.760
Oh, um, of course.

00:14:27.880 --> 00:14:33.500
<i>The way Jonas behaves is probably 
the correct way to act as a fairy's master...</i>

00:14:33.500 --> 00:14:34.470
<i>but even so...</i>

00:14:34.470 --> 00:14:38.540
The ability to erase her form? 
That's pretty impressive.

00:14:38.540 --> 00:14:41.610
But compared to the power of 
the wonder that is me, it's still lacking.

00:14:43.030 --> 00:14:45.420
Mithril, what powers do you have?

00:14:46.000 --> 00:14:47.260
Don't be too surprised!

00:14:47.260 --> 00:14:50.360
In the northernmost part of 
the Kingdom of Highland lies a great lake,

00:14:50.360 --> 00:14:51.760
the waters of Loess Lake...

00:14:51.760 --> 00:14:55.390
A drop of that water landed on a leaf, 
and that's what I was born from!

00:14:55.390 --> 00:14:56.720
From a water drop?

00:14:56.720 --> 00:14:59.160
Are all fairies born from water drops?

00:14:59.160 --> 00:15:01.630
Anne, you don't know anything, do you?

00:15:01.980 --> 00:15:04.620
Fairies are born from all sorts of things.

00:15:05.970 --> 00:15:07.500
Grass seeds. The fruit or nuts of trees.

00:15:07.500 --> 00:15:09.200
Water drops or jewels.

00:15:09.200 --> 00:15:11.780
The energy of an object 
condenses and then we're born.

00:15:12.260 --> 00:15:15.470
But for that to happen, 
the gaze of a living being is needed.

00:15:15.470 --> 00:15:18.220
Human, animal, it doesn't matter what.

00:15:18.220 --> 00:15:21.190
Being gazed upon 
causes the energy to take form,

00:15:21.190 --> 00:15:23.350
and that's what turns into a fairy.

00:15:24.990 --> 00:15:26.170
Really?

00:15:26.170 --> 00:15:27.900
Challe, what were you born from?

00:15:29.110 --> 00:15:31.930
From the look of him, I'd say obsidian.

00:15:31.930 --> 00:15:35.950
Incidentally, precious stone fairies 
have the power to create sharp things.

00:15:35.950 --> 00:15:39.500
Since I was born from a water drop, 
I can control water.

00:15:39.500 --> 00:15:41.080
That's my power.

00:15:41.080 --> 00:15:42.160
Control water?

00:15:42.160 --> 00:15:43.790
That's incredible! Will you show me?

00:15:43.790 --> 00:15:44.970
Sure!

00:15:47.880 --> 00:15:48.760
There!

00:15:51.070 --> 00:15:52.030
That's cold!

00:15:52.030 --> 00:15:53.840
You're amazing, Mithril!

00:15:53.840 --> 00:15:55.720
What can you do, using that?

00:15:55.720 --> 00:15:58.180
What? I just showed you.

00:15:58.180 --> 00:16:00.270
What? That's all?

00:16:00.270 --> 00:16:02.860
What do you mean, 
"That's all"?! "That's all"?!

00:16:02.860 --> 00:16:05.420
Are you criticizing the power 
of the wonder that is me?

00:16:05.420 --> 00:16:08.360
It would be useful 
in giving water to little birds.

00:16:08.360 --> 00:16:11.400
N-No one asked you! 
And what kind of comment is that?

00:16:11.400 --> 00:16:13.040
Are you making fun of me?

00:16:13.040 --> 00:16:13.580
This is bad.

00:16:13.580 --> 00:16:14.410
What?

00:16:14.410 --> 00:16:15.930
What's bad?

00:16:17.380 --> 00:16:20.120
Hey, Challe fen Challe, that's...

00:16:20.120 --> 00:16:22.060
What? What's wrong?

00:16:22.060 --> 00:16:23.850
Anne! Look above!

00:16:27.920 --> 00:16:29.630
Is this an attack?

00:16:30.200 --> 00:16:33.520
Wild crows are cleaners, 
scavenging the wilds for carrion.

00:16:33.520 --> 00:16:36.060
But when there is no carrion for them to eat,

00:16:36.060 --> 00:16:37.920
they form large flocks to hunt down prey...

00:16:37.920 --> 00:16:39.350
and devour it alive.

00:16:40.120 --> 00:16:43.260
The day before yesterday, 
they barely had a lick of bandit blood.

00:16:43.260 --> 00:16:44.810
It must have made them hungry.

00:16:47.150 --> 00:16:48.490
Challe, please...

00:16:50.720 --> 00:16:52.440
Challe, I'm giving you an order.

00:16:52.440 --> 00:16:55.180
Protect us from the wild crows!

00:16:55.180 --> 00:16:57.340
I hold your wing.

00:16:57.340 --> 00:16:59.660
You know what that means, don't you?

00:17:00.930 --> 00:17:02.370
Stop the cart.

00:17:03.630 --> 00:17:05.290
Hide in the cargo hold.

00:17:05.290 --> 00:17:06.200
Anne!

00:17:06.200 --> 00:17:09.250
Jonas, you should hide 
in your cargo hold, too! Quickly!

00:17:09.250 --> 00:17:11.870
I see! So this is what returning a favor is!

00:17:11.870 --> 00:17:13.290
I will chase them off and—

00:17:13.290 --> 00:17:14.220
You too!

00:17:25.420 --> 00:17:27.480
<i>Help me, Challe!</i>

00:17:27.480 --> 00:17:30.190
Don't be afraid, Anne. It's all right.

00:17:30.620 --> 00:17:32.860
Challe fen Challe is obsidian!

00:17:32.860 --> 00:17:34.190
He isn't like us.

00:17:35.450 --> 00:17:37.180
He won't get hurt...

00:17:37.180 --> 00:17:38.390
and he won't break.

00:17:42.600 --> 00:17:43.980
Is it over?

00:17:51.530 --> 00:17:52.500
Challe...

00:18:05.560 --> 00:18:06.680
Did your legs give out on you?

00:18:07.240 --> 00:18:08.900
N-No, they didn't!

00:18:12.320 --> 00:18:14.520
What's wrong, Scarecrow?

00:18:14.520 --> 00:18:16.610
Are you requesting 
a more special sort of service?

00:18:20.050 --> 00:18:21.570
I-I would never!

00:18:22.530 --> 00:18:26.250
A-At any rate, thank you. For saving me.

00:18:29.670 --> 00:18:32.880
This isn't good. 
It's just one thing after another.

00:18:32.880 --> 00:18:34.830
What's wrong, Anne?

00:18:34.830 --> 00:18:37.720
We won't reach the fortshelter before sunset.

00:18:37.720 --> 00:18:40.620
The wild crow's attack 
has made a mess of our schedule.

00:18:40.620 --> 00:18:41.590
Oh, wait!

00:18:42.030 --> 00:18:43.320
There's a doctor's inn!

00:18:43.320 --> 00:18:45.060
What is a doctor's inn?

00:18:45.060 --> 00:18:49.470
Just as the name states, it's an inn 
where doctors allow travelers to stay.

00:18:49.470 --> 00:18:52.220
And bandits rarely attack doctors.

00:18:52.220 --> 00:18:55.650
For travelers, they're the next 
safest place to fortshelters.

00:18:55.650 --> 00:18:58.860
Will such an old map 
really prove to be accurate?

00:18:59.210 --> 00:19:01.320
There are no mistakes 
in a map that Mama drew!

00:19:03.240 --> 00:19:05.280
In any case, that is where we'll stay today.

00:19:05.280 --> 00:19:06.490
We have to hurry!

00:19:09.880 --> 00:19:11.900
<i>Please let us make it in time.</i>

00:19:13.570 --> 00:19:14.740
<i>Is it impossible?</i>

00:19:15.700 --> 00:19:18.420
<i>Mama would have been 
able to do this properly.</i>

00:19:18.920 --> 00:19:21.510
Where is this mother of yours?

00:19:23.090 --> 00:19:26.640
Mama died. Did I not mention it?

00:19:27.380 --> 00:19:28.650
Two weeks ago.

00:19:29.360 --> 00:19:32.580
I made up my mind to become 
a silver sugar master, like she was.

00:19:33.070 --> 00:19:35.680
At the end of autumn, 
there's an event held in Lewiston,

00:19:35.680 --> 00:19:38.190
the Sugar Confectionary Exhibition. 
I'll submit a piece...

00:19:38.190 --> 00:19:39.930
and have the king acknowledge my skills.

00:19:40.800 --> 00:19:43.390
I want to become 
a silver sugar master this year.

00:19:43.390 --> 00:19:44.990
Do you know why?

00:19:47.320 --> 00:19:49.720
In the winter, we celebrate Pull Soul Day.

00:19:49.720 --> 00:19:53.420
We send off those who died that year
 as they're pulled to the heavens.

00:19:53.850 --> 00:19:58.630
As a silver sugar master, I will make 
a splendid sugar confection with my own hands,

00:19:58.630 --> 00:20:01.540
and send Mama's spirit to the heavens.

00:20:02.040 --> 00:20:05.610
That way, Mama will feel reassured 
and be able to go to the heavens, won't she?

00:20:05.610 --> 00:20:07.350
It's a good idea, don't you think?

00:20:07.780 --> 00:20:09.460
<i>And that's why, is it?</i>

00:20:10.310 --> 00:20:11.770
Oh! A light!

00:20:13.280 --> 00:20:15.370
Wait! Please wait!

00:20:18.050 --> 00:20:21.650
Wild crows? That's quite the calamity.

00:20:21.650 --> 00:20:23.450
The important thing is that you're safe.

00:20:23.450 --> 00:20:26.620
This room is for you and yours. 
Your travel companions are next door.

00:20:26.620 --> 00:20:30.400
Leave your things and, once you've 
rested a bit, come to the dining hall.

00:20:30.400 --> 00:20:33.620
We should be able to serve you 
something like a simple soup.

00:20:36.100 --> 00:20:38.540
A bed. It's been a while.

00:20:39.220 --> 00:20:40.100
Anne.

00:20:40.830 --> 00:20:43.470
You're hungry, aren't you? 
Let's go and accept their offer of food.

00:20:43.770 --> 00:20:47.300
Jonas... I'll rest a little more first.

00:20:47.300 --> 00:20:49.550
There's no need to pretend you're all right.

00:20:49.550 --> 00:20:51.680
You're starving, aren't you? Come on.

00:20:59.230 --> 00:21:04.990
The Bloody Highway

00:22:35.620 --> 00:22:40.040
<b>The Sugar Apple is the Tree of Betrayal</b>
